# Authentic voice (named speaker / legacy “mind” output)

**Not fork doctrine** — Record/gate rules: [`docs/archive/grace-mar.md`](../../docs/archive/grace-mar.md) · [`docs/agent-rules/deep-rules.md`](../../docs/agent-rules/deep-rules.md).

When the operator or task calls for a **named speaker lens** (Mercouris, Mearsheimer, Barnes, …) or any response grounded in a **`statecraft/voices/<speaker>-profile.md`**, the agent **must** render analysis **in that speaker’s authentic register** — not a neutral third-person précis (“Mearsheimer would say…”) as a substitute for **in-voice** prose.

**Voices supersede minds:** [VOICES-SUPERSEDE-MINDS.md](../../docs/archive/skill-work-legacy/work-strategy/VOICES-SUPERSEDE-MINDS.md). **`strategy-expert-*-mind.md`** / **`CIV-MIND-*`** are compatibility redirects and quote banks — **not** primary SSOT for new work.

**`tri-mind` / `tri-frame` choreography is deprecated** — see [TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md](../../docs/archive/skill-work-legacy/work-strategy/TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md). Structured comparison → **`state-synthesis`**, **`primary-overhearing-analysis`**, or **[`periodic-statecraft-review` runbook](../../skills/runbooks/periodic-statecraft-review.runbook.md)** (`statecraft-multi-lens` archived).

**Default:** There is **no** opt-out from authentic voice for named-speaker blocks. Rubrics or diff tables go **after** in-voice material — **never** as a replacement.

## Triggers (non-exhaustive)

- **Explicit:** **Mercouris** / **Mearsheimer** / **Barnes** (or other mapped speaker) as the **requested single lens**, post-entry lens picks from **`strategy`** / **`skill-strategy`**
- **Implicit:** Answering in a speaker’s style after reading their **voice profile** (or legacy mind file only when profile is Tier B)
- **Deprecated (redirect):** `tri-mind`, `tri-frame`, `tutti`, **`ab+c`** → [TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md](../../docs/archive/skill-work-legacy/work-strategy/TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md)

